On Jul 5, 10:29 pm, Kent Paul Dolan <xanth...@well.com> wrote:
> A warning not yet seen: be careful with force bolt,
> so as not to break nymph-carried mirrors and nerf
> your luck. The thing about bad luck is you don't see
> that it is what is really killing you when you're
> dying, so avoiding it is a hard lesson to learn.

There are so many things that can go wrong with force bolt. I hate it
when I accidentally blow the door off a shop, especially in the mines.
If I'm not able to flee or take out a shopkeeper at that point, I
usually quit to avoid leaving a bad bones.

Bad luck is easily fixable in sokoban but it can be difficult to make
it there alive if your character is already in a bad way.

One of the more subtle problems about playing wizards is that you can
gain levels super quickly without gaining much survivability. Being at
7th level after running around casting force bolt for a while is just
plain bad for you if you don't have an improved AC, because you get
more difficult wandering monsters, and it's only a matter of time
until a bunch of ants hems you in or you run into a horse. Meanwhile,
those extra levels don't help your spellcasting significantly if you
don't have the wisdom to make use of the extra power. Wizard HP are so
low that it almost doesn't matter how many you have until you have a
negative AC because anything other than a lichen can kill you in a
turn or three. Rely on the pet(s) and wait until you have the right
things in your inventory (including escape items) before starting to
play aggressively.



